H2 — Section Heading:
Frequently Asked Questions — Excavation & Site Preparation


Q1 — How much does excavation cost in Barrie, Ontario?
Excavation costs in Barrie depend on the depth, soil conditions, site access, and the scope of the project. Residential foundation digs typically run between $3,000 and $15,000 or more depending on the size. Pool excavation usually falls in the $2,000 to $8,000 range. The best way to get an accurate number is a free on-site estimate — contact us and we'll come out and give you a real price.


Q2 — Do you need a permit for excavation in Barrie or Simcoe County?
Most structural excavation — foundations, large grading projects, and septic work — requires a building permit through the City of Barrie or your local municipality. Any trenching for utilities also requires underground locates through Ontario One Call (1-800-400-2255) before any digging starts. We can walk you through what's required for your specific project.


Q3 — What areas do you serve for excavation and site preparation?
We serve Barrie, Orillia, Innisfil, Wasaga Beach, Angus, Springwater, Essa, Oro-Medonte, Collingwood, Midland, Bradford, and throughout Simcoe County, Ontario. If you're not sure whether we cover your area, just call — if we can get a machine there, we'll make it work.


Q4 — What is hydro vacuum excavation and when is it needed?
Hydrovac uses pressurized water to break up soil and an industrial vacuum to remove it — without ever touching buried utilities with a bucket or blade. It's required whenever you're working near existing underground services like gas lines, water mains, fibre optic cables, or hydro infrastructure. Municipalities, engineers, and utility companies increasingly require it for all work within utility corridors. We offer hydrovac throughout Simcoe County.


Q5 — What is a lot grading certificate and do I need one in Barrie?
A lot grading certificate confirms that your property drains the way the municipality approved. It shows that water flows away from your house toward the right catch basins and swales. Most municipalities in Simcoe County — including Barrie, Innisfil, Orillia, and Wasaga Beach — require this certificate before they'll issue your occupancy permit. We do final lot grading to meet municipal standards and can coordinate the certification through a licensed grading inspector.


